NAME
       driver_ctl - inspect and control device drivers

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/syscall.h>

       syscall3(SYS_DRIVER_CTL, op, arg, value);

DESCRIPTION
       Operation 0 fills an array of driver records: the name, whether
       anything on this machine matched, whether the probe succeeded,
       how many devices were claimed, the vendor and device id of the
       first, when it started, and whether it is probed at boot.

       Operation 1 probes the hardware again with the named driver.
       Operation 2 shuts it down, which only drivers carrying a stop
       function can do. Operation 3 sets whether it is tried when a
       matching device appears.

       Listing is open to anyone; the rest require root.

RETURN VALUE
       Listing returns the number of drivers. The others return 0, or a
       negative value: -1 no such driver, -2 nothing matched or the
       driver cannot stop, -3 the probe or the stop failed.

SEE ALSO
       drv(1), lspci(2), sysreport(1)
